1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,280
March 12, 2014.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:05,864
Federal agents begin a month-long hunt for

3
00:00:05,864 --> 00:00:08,339
members of one gang alliance.

4
00:00:08,789 --> 00:00:11,858
Dallas. San Antonio. Baltimore. New York.

5
00:00:11,858 --> 00:00:12,757
Los Angeles.

6
00:00:13,207 --> 00:00:17,547
By April 13, they have arrested 638 gang

7
00:00:17,547 --> 00:00:22,538
members and associates, from 145 gangs, in 179

8
00:00:22,538 --> 00:00:23,297
cities.

9
00:00:23,747 --> 00:00:26,585
Most of them claim the same name. Sureños.

10
00:00:26,585 --> 00:00:27,395
Southerners.

11
00:00:27,845 --> 00:00:30,886
How did a network born on the streets of

12
00:00:30,886 --> 00:00:34,002
Southern California end up in 179 cities?

13
00:00:34,002 --> 00:00:35,675
And who was it paying?

14
00:00:36,275 --> 00:00:38,579
This is the case of the Sureños.

15
00:00:41,179 --> 00:00:43,611
The Sureños are not one gang.

16
00:00:44,061 --> 00:00:47,495
In 2014, the head of ICE investigations in Los

17
00:00:47,495 --> 00:00:50,333
Angeles called them an umbrella group.

18
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:53,767
According to ICE, they are made up of hundreds

19
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:56,754
of cliques across the country, under one

20
00:00:56,754 --> 00:00:57,949
southern banner.

21
00:00:58,399 --> 00:01:01,278
What ties them together is a prison gang.

22
00:01:01,278 --> 00:01:02,542
The Mexican Mafia.

23
00:01:02,542 --> 00:01:04,649
Known as La Eme. The letter M.

24
00:01:05,099 --> 00:01:08,874
According to Police Magazine, it was formed in

25
00:01:08,874 --> 00:01:12,566
1957, at a state prison in Tracy, California.

26
00:01:13,016 --> 00:01:15,615
M is the 13th letter of the alphabet.

27
00:01:15,615 --> 00:01:18,635
When a Southern California street gang adds

28
00:01:18,635 --> 00:01:21,585
the number 13 to its name, it is declaring

29
00:01:21,585 --> 00:01:23,832
allegiance to the Mexican Mafia.

30
00:01:24,282 --> 00:01:27,704
According to ICE, the Sureños pay tribute to

31
00:01:27,704 --> 00:01:29,103
the Mexican Mafia.

32
00:01:29,553 --> 00:01:32,104
California has a second alliance.

33
00:01:32,104 --> 00:01:35,350
In the north, the Norteños, aligned with a

34
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:38,364
rival prison gang, the Nuestra Familia.

35
00:01:38,814 --> 00:01:41,370
The state's attorney general reported that

36
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:43,987
these two alliances account for the largest

37
00:01:43,987 --> 00:01:46,665
number of street gang members in California.

38
00:01:47,665 --> 00:01:50,975
To see how the system works, look at one gang.

39
00:01:50,975 --> 00:01:51,910
Florencia 13.

40
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:55,424
According to the indictment, Florencia 13

41
00:01:55,424 --> 00:01:58,862
controlled drug distribution in unincorporated

42
00:01:58,862 --> 00:02:02,300
areas south of Los Angeles, and in cities like

43
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:03,496
Huntington Park.

44
00:02:03,946 --> 00:02:06,600
According to the indictments, the gang was

45
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:09,065
controlled by a Mexican Mafia member in

46
00:02:09,065 --> 00:02:12,287
prison, and by Mexican Mafia members on the street.

47
00:02:12,737 --> 00:02:15,421
Its leaders collected what investigators

48
00:02:15,421 --> 00:02:16,226
called rent.

49
00:02:16,226 --> 00:02:19,245
From gang members, and from others committing

50
00:02:19,245 --> 00:02:21,325
crimes in the gang's territory.

51
00:02:21,325 --> 00:02:24,076
In exchange, the payers got Mexican Mafia

52
00:02:24,076 --> 00:02:27,095
protection, when they went to jail or prison.

53
00:02:27,545 --> 00:02:30,762
Prosecutors alleged that the gang ran drug

54
00:02:30,762 --> 00:02:33,750
distribution dens in South Los Angeles.

55
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:37,198
And the DEA said Florencia 13 was involved in

56
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:40,569
shootings of African-Americans, in the areas

57
00:02:40,569 --> 00:02:41,411
it claimed.

58
00:02:41,861 --> 00:02:45,398
A task force spent three years on the case.

59
00:02:45,398 --> 00:02:48,852
Sheriff's deputies, the DEA, ATF, ICE, the

60
00:02:48,852 --> 00:02:52,389
FBI, LAPD, the IRS, and probation officers.

61
00:02:52,389 --> 00:02:55,515
They called it Operation Joker's Wild.

62
00:02:55,965 --> 00:02:59,495
In the fall of 2007, a federal grand jury

63
00:02:59,495 --> 00:03:01,734
returned four indictments.

64
00:03:01,734 --> 00:03:03,026
102 defendants.

65
00:03:03,476 --> 00:03:05,274
The arrests came in waves.

66
00:03:05,274 --> 00:03:07,765
The first phase came in mid-October.

67
00:03:07,765 --> 00:03:09,909
Two weeks later, a second wave.

68
00:03:09,909 --> 00:03:12,607
By then, 80 defendants were in custody.

69
00:03:13,057 --> 00:03:13,619
The U.S.

70
00:03:13,619 --> 00:03:16,785
attorney in Los Angeles, Thomas O'Brien, said

71
00:03:16,785 --> 00:03:19,950
more than 100 people linked to the gang faced

72
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:23,467
federal charges, and up to life in federal prison.

73
00:03:23,917 --> 00:03:26,896
The Los Angeles County sheriff, Lee Baca, sent

74
00:03:26,896 --> 00:03:27,544
a message.

75
00:03:27,994 --> 00:03:29,802
In January 2009, after a

76
00:03:29,802 --> 00:03:33,269
three-and-a-half-month trial, a jury convicted

77
00:03:33,269 --> 00:03:35,303
ten members and associates.

78
00:03:35,303 --> 00:03:38,166
Racketeering, drugs, and in some cases

79
00:03:38,166 --> 00:03:39,749
conspiracy to murder.

80
00:03:40,199 --> 00:03:43,279
By then, 76 defendants had been convicted.

81
00:03:43,279 --> 00:03:46,653
The DEA called it the largest gang takedown in

82
00:03:46,653 --> 00:03:47,900
American history.

83
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:52,207
But the Sureños were not staying in Los Angeles.

84
00:03:52,657 --> 00:03:56,062
In 2011, the FBI's National Gang Intelligence

85
00:03:56,062 --> 00:03:59,014
Center published its threat assessment.

86
00:03:59,014 --> 00:04:02,192
It said Sureño gangs were expanding faster

87
00:04:02,192 --> 00:04:04,614
than other national-level gangs.

88
00:04:04,614 --> 00:04:07,035
In membership, and in geography.

89
00:04:07,485 --> 00:04:10,310
20 states and the District of Columbia

90
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:14,027
reported more Sureño migration into their regions.

91
00:04:14,027 --> 00:04:17,446
Gangs moved into Northern California, and into

92
00:04:17,446 --> 00:04:19,453
Arizona, Nevada and Oregon.

93
00:04:19,903 --> 00:04:22,780
The report also listed Sureños among gangs

94
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:24,971
tied to Mexican drug trafficking

95
00:04:24,971 --> 00:04:27,985
organizations, among gangs involved in human

96
00:04:27,985 --> 00:04:31,066
trafficking, and among gangs with members who

97
00:04:31,066 --> 00:04:33,258
had served in the U.S. military.

98
00:04:33,708 --> 00:04:37,208
The same report said Sureños in California and

99
00:04:37,208 --> 00:04:40,708
South Carolina were associated with the Zetas,

100
00:04:40,708 --> 00:04:44,588
a Mexican drug cartel, according to 2010 reporting.

101
00:04:45,038 --> 00:04:48,383
By 2014, ICE estimated the Sureños had more

102
00:04:48,383 --> 00:04:51,884
than 30,000 members in the United States, and

103
00:04:51,884 --> 00:04:54,062
said the number was growing.

104
00:04:54,512 --> 00:04:58,343
For scale, the same FBI report estimated about

105
00:04:58,343 --> 00:05:02,008
1.4 million gang members nationwide, in more

106
00:05:02,008 --> 00:05:03,507
than 33,000 gangs.

107
00:05:03,507 --> 00:05:07,339
It warned that these totals are estimates, not

108
00:05:07,339 --> 00:05:08,421
exact counts.

109
00:05:08,871 --> 00:05:11,998
In a Texas town north of Houston, an agent

110
00:05:11,998 --> 00:05:15,869
points out the mark on a utility pole. S-U-R. South.

111
00:05:16,319 --> 00:05:19,193
To federal investigators, a southern gang this

112
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:21,567
spread out needed a national response.

113
00:05:22,567 --> 00:05:25,660
That response came in the spring of 2014.

114
00:05:26,110 --> 00:05:29,080
Homeland Security Investigations, the

115
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:32,532
investigative arm of ICE, ran the operation

116
00:05:32,532 --> 00:05:35,984
with 150 federal, state and local partners.

117
00:05:35,984 --> 00:05:38,633
It was called Project Southbound.

118
00:05:39,083 --> 00:05:41,790
It ran from March 12 to April 13.

119
00:05:41,790 --> 00:05:44,908
ICE's top official at the time, Thomas

120
00:05:44,908 --> 00:05:48,683
Winkowski, called it the largest ICE operation

121
00:05:48,683 --> 00:05:50,816
ever aimed at the Sureños.

122
00:05:51,266 --> 00:05:54,562
Teams gear up in parking lots. Vests. Radios.

123
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:55,661
Lists of names.

124
00:05:56,111 --> 00:05:58,799
In Dallas, officers from the city's police

125
00:05:58,799 --> 00:06:01,423
department work alongside federal agents.

126
00:06:01,873 --> 00:06:04,765
In Baltimore, agents go door to door.

127
00:06:04,765 --> 00:06:08,127
In Maryland, nine members of MS-13, another

128
00:06:08,127 --> 00:06:11,644
gang that claims the number 13, were arrested

129
00:06:11,644 --> 00:06:13,521
on racketeering charges.

130
00:06:13,971 --> 00:06:16,316
In Los Angeles, the head of ICE

131
00:06:16,316 --> 00:06:19,646
investigations, Claude Arnold, said 132 gang

132
00:06:19,646 --> 00:06:22,824
members were taken off the city's streets.

133
00:06:23,274 --> 00:06:26,837
He explained why agents go after individual members.

134
00:06:27,287 --> 00:06:31,213
When it was over, ICE counted 757 arrests.

135
00:06:31,213 --> 00:06:34,671
638 were gang members and associates.

136
00:06:34,671 --> 00:06:39,532
More than 73 percent of those arrested were Sureños.

137
00:06:39,982 --> 00:06:42,836
414 had violent criminal histories.

138
00:06:42,836 --> 00:06:45,202
Seven were wanted for murder.

139
00:06:45,202 --> 00:06:47,811
Five for rape or sexual assault.

140
00:06:48,261 --> 00:06:50,925
525 faced criminal charges.

141
00:06:50,925 --> 00:06:55,267
113 were arrested on immigration violations.

142
00:06:55,267 --> 00:06:57,931
256 were foreign nationals.

143
00:06:57,931 --> 00:07:01,680
Those arrested came from 21 countries.

144
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:06,745
Agents also seized 54 guns, drugs, and more

145
00:07:06,745 --> 00:07:09,106
than $166,000 in cash.

146
00:07:10,106 --> 00:07:13,558
In San Francisco, a father and son were

147
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:17,010
arrested on state drug and gun charges.

148
00:07:17,010 --> 00:07:20,462
Agents seized more than 4,600 marijuana

149
00:07:20,462 --> 00:07:24,445
plants, an AR-15 rifle, a stolen handgun, and

150
00:07:24,445 --> 00:07:26,746
more than $85,000 in cash.

151
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:30,911
At the time, ICE said its gang program had

152
00:07:30,911 --> 00:07:34,626
arrested more than 33,000 gang members and

153
00:07:34,626 --> 00:07:39,049
associates since 2005, from more than 2,600 gangs.

154
00:07:39,049 --> 00:07:42,321
Including more than 438 gang leaders.

155
00:07:43,321 --> 00:07:45,327
Two years later, they did it again.

156
00:07:45,777 --> 00:07:50,224
From February 15 to March 21, 2016, HSI ran a

157
00:07:50,224 --> 00:07:54,374
five-week surge called Project Shadowfire.

158
00:07:54,824 --> 00:07:59,319
Most of those arrested were tied to MS-13. Sureños.

159
00:07:59,319 --> 00:08:00,817
Norteños. Bloods.

160
00:08:00,817 --> 00:08:03,549
And several prison-based gangs.

161
00:08:03,999 --> 00:08:06,439
The numbers were bigger.

162
00:08:06,439 --> 00:08:07,861
1,133 arrests.

163
00:08:07,861 --> 00:08:11,622
915 were gang members and associates.

164
00:08:11,622 --> 00:08:14,773
1,001 were charged with crimes.

165
00:08:15,223 --> 00:08:18,590
And here is a detail that often gets lost.

166
00:08:18,590 --> 00:08:22,278
ICE said most of the people arrested were U.S.

167
00:08:22,278 --> 00:08:22,999
citizens.

168
00:08:22,999 --> 00:08:25,164
239 were foreign nationals.

169
00:08:25,614 --> 00:08:28,450
The charges included drug trafficking, human

170
00:08:28,450 --> 00:08:31,801
smuggling, sex trafficking, murder and racketeering.

171
00:08:32,251 --> 00:08:35,317
The most activity was in Los Angeles, San

172
00:08:35,317 --> 00:08:39,056
Juan, Atlanta, San Francisco, Houston and El Paso.

173
00:08:39,506 --> 00:08:43,065
Agents seized 150 firearms, more than 20

174
00:08:43,065 --> 00:08:46,802
kilograms of drugs, and more than $70,000.

175
00:08:47,252 --> 00:08:50,343
Both operations ran under one umbrella

176
00:08:50,343 --> 00:08:53,272
program, Operation Community Shield.

177
00:08:53,272 --> 00:08:56,770
ICE said that since 2005 it had led to more

178
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:59,455
than 40,000 gang-related arrests.

179
00:09:00,455 --> 00:09:03,047
Arrests take gang members off the street.

180
00:09:03,047 --> 00:09:05,703
Racketeering cases go after the structure.

181
00:09:06,153 --> 00:09:09,597
In August 2013, Florencia 13 was back in

182
00:09:09,597 --> 00:09:10,802
federal court.

183
00:09:10,802 --> 00:09:14,763
A racketeering indictment named 30 members and

184
00:09:14,763 --> 00:09:15,710
associates.

185
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:18,568
The case showed how the gang ran.

186
00:09:18,568 --> 00:09:21,705
One woman, Giselle Casado, was described by

187
00:09:21,705 --> 00:09:24,624
prosecutors as a secretary to the gang's

188
00:09:24,624 --> 00:09:25,499
shot-caller.

189
00:09:25,499 --> 00:09:28,636
She relayed messages, controlled money, and

190
00:09:28,636 --> 00:09:30,752
helped with drug trafficking.

191
00:09:30,752 --> 00:09:32,139
She got 121 months.

192
00:09:32,589 --> 00:09:35,861
A man prosecutors called one of the gang's

193
00:09:35,861 --> 00:09:38,821
soldiers, Jose Sanchez, provided armed

194
00:09:38,821 --> 00:09:41,314
security at the gambling houses.

195
00:09:41,314 --> 00:09:44,819
The judge said he had consistently led a life

196
00:09:44,819 --> 00:09:46,455
of crime. 238 months.

197
00:09:46,905 --> 00:09:49,977
According to trial evidence, in March 2010, a

198
00:09:49,977 --> 00:09:53,049
senior member of the gang, who was in custody

199
00:09:53,049 --> 00:09:56,053
at the time, ordered two members to beat and

200
00:09:56,053 --> 00:09:57,487
kill a junior member.

201
00:09:57,487 --> 00:10:00,422
Within hours, the victim was attacked in an

202
00:10:00,422 --> 00:10:03,972
alley in Huntington Park, and later shot and killed.

203
00:10:04,422 --> 00:10:07,468
The two men ordered to carry it out, Jose

204
00:10:07,468 --> 00:10:11,184
Dorado and Tannous Fazah, were convicted at trial.

205
00:10:11,184 --> 00:10:14,230
In June 2017, they were sentenced to life

206
00:10:14,230 --> 00:10:15,345
without parole.

207
00:10:15,795 --> 00:10:18,899
Prosecutors wrote in their sentencing papers,

208
00:10:18,899 --> 00:10:21,866
there is no crime more serious than murder.

209
00:10:21,866 --> 00:10:24,833
By then, 25 defendants in the case had been

210
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:25,523
convicted.

211
00:10:25,973 --> 00:10:28,250
The pattern has not gone away.

212
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:31,665
In March 2026, a federal judge in Los Angeles

213
00:10:31,665 --> 00:10:35,080
sentenced a full member of the Mexican Mafia,

214
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:37,813
Michael Lerma, known as Pomona Mike.

215
00:10:38,263 --> 00:10:41,331
Prosecutors said that from 2012 to 2020, he

216
00:10:41,331 --> 00:10:44,613
controlled and extorted drug money from Latino

217
00:10:44,613 --> 00:10:47,752
street gangs around Pomona, and from inmates

218
00:10:47,752 --> 00:10:49,036
in a state prison.

219
00:10:49,486 --> 00:10:52,839
In June 2020, prosecutors said, he directed

220
00:10:52,839 --> 00:10:56,425
three Pomona gang members to kill a man inside

221
00:10:56,425 --> 00:10:59,700
a federal jail in Los Angeles, over unpaid

222
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,558
drug debts.

223
00:11:01,008 --> 00:11:03,688
A jury convicted Lerma and three others.

224
00:11:03,688 --> 00:11:07,037
All four were sentenced to life in federal prison.

225
00:11:07,037 --> 00:11:10,052
Prosecutors wrote that his role reflected his

226
00:11:10,052 --> 00:11:12,464
cruelty, his cunning, and his power.

227
00:11:12,914 --> 00:11:16,141
Prosecutors have won nine convictions in that

228
00:11:16,141 --> 00:11:17,002
case so far.

229
00:11:17,002 --> 00:11:20,230
The FBI's San Gabriel Valley task force, with

230
00:11:20,230 --> 00:11:23,314
the sheriff's department, local police, and

231
00:11:23,314 --> 00:11:24,605
the DEA, built it.

232
00:11:25,605 --> 00:11:28,139
2007. 2014. 2016. 2026.

233
00:11:28,139 --> 00:11:32,877
Different operations, different defendants.

234
00:11:32,877 --> 00:11:34,970
The same structure.

235
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:36,979
A prison gang at the top.

236
00:11:36,979 --> 00:11:39,099
Hundreds of street gangs below it.

237
00:11:39,099 --> 00:11:41,905
And the money that flows up, from the streets

238
00:11:41,905 --> 00:11:42,716
to the cells.

239
00:11:43,166 --> 00:11:44,734
A letter of the alphabet.

240
00:11:44,734 --> 00:11:45,925
A number on a wall.

241
00:11:45,925 --> 00:11:48,371
And the people who keep taking it down.

242
00:11:49,171 --> 00:11:51,128
Case file 006. Closed.

243
00:11:51,128 --> 00:11:54,419
The next file is already on the desk.
